---
import CouchpilotLayout from '../../layouts/CouchpilotLayout.astro';
const h2 = 'text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 pt-6';
---

<CouchpilotLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Terms of Use | Couchpilot"
  description="Terms of use for the Couchpilot app: free recommendations, third-party streaming data without guarantee, and the Couchpilot Pro subscription."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-6 pt-10 pb-24 max-w-4xl text-slate-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-8">TERMS OF USE</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-slate-500 font-medium">Last updated: 2026-11-15</p>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-lg">
      <p>
        These terms apply to the app Couchpilot (package and bundle ID <code>com.cmart.couchpilot</code>). By using the
        app you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>1. Provider</h2>
      <p>
        Christoph Martin<br />
        Fischerweg 8, 7503 Großpetersdorf, Austria<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@endure-cycling.com" class="cp-accent">info@endure-cycling.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>2. What Couchpilot does</h2>
      <p>
        Couchpilot recommends films and series based on your ratings and shows where they stream, can be rented or
        bought. The app is free and works without an account. Couchpilot does not stream any content itself; you watch
        on the provider's own service.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>3. Data from third parties</h2>
      <p>
        Availability, prices, top 10 lists, scores and descriptions come from third parties: the Streaming Availability
        API by Movie of the Night, Trakt, Wikidata and Wikipedia. Providers change their catalogs and prices often, so
        this information can be out of date or wrong. Check the provider's offer before you subscribe, rent or buy. We
        don't guarantee that a title is available or that a price is correct. Links to providers can be affiliate links.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>4. Couchpilot Pro</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
        <li>Couchpilot Pro is an optional subscription, sold monthly or yearly through the App Store or Google Play.
          The app shows the price before you buy.</li>
        <li>New subscribers get a free trial when the app offers one (currently 7 days). If you don't cancel during the
          trial, the paid subscription starts.</li>
        <li>The subscription renews automatically unless you cancel it at least 24 hours before the end of the current
          period. Cancel in your App Store or Google Play account settings. Deleting the app does not cancel it.</li>
        <li>Payment, refunds and cancellation are handled by Apple or Google under their terms. We can't issue refunds
          ourselves.</li>
        <li>Pro features are described on the paywall in the app. We may improve or change them; if we remove a paid
          feature, you can cancel the subscription.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class={h2}>5. Account</h2>
      <p>
        Signing in with Apple or Google is optional. You can delete your account and all data in the app under Profile.
        How we handle data is described in the <a href="/couchpilot/privacy/" class="cp-accent">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>6. Fair use</h2>
      <p>
        Don't access the app's servers automatically (scripts, scraping) and don't use the app in a way that harms the
        service or other users. We may block access in case of misuse.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>7. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        We are liable without limitation for intent and gross negligence and for injury to life, body or health. For
        slight negligence we are liable only for breaches of essential obligations and only for typical, foreseeable
        damage. Mandatory consumer protection law stays unaffected.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>8. App Store version</h2>
      <p>
        For the version from Apple's App Store, Apple's
        <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" class="cp-accent">standard licence
        agreement (EULA)</a> applies in addition to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>9. Changes and applicable law</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms; the date above shows the current version. Austrian law applies. If you are a
        consumer, the mandatory consumer protection rules of the country you live in stay in force.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</CouchpilotLayout>
